Subject: [PATCH 02390/11362] [conductor] Pre-gate block: PHASE A2 (HEADLINE
 skeptic-proofing; GATED on exp4348 s3_guided_beats_control==true) -- PAPO
 REWARD-STATE-ALIGNMENT DIAGNOSTIC (arXiv:2606.08501 VERIFIED 'Back on Track:
 Aligning Rewards and States for Reasoning in Diffusion LLMs'). IF exp4348
 shows an S3 generation gain, the operator (twice-burned on DiffusionGemma
 over-claims, .396/.397) will ask: is the gain from rewards aligned to
 AUTHENTIC denoising states, or an artifact of remasking / position cues / the
 scorer correlating with something other than process quality? PAPO is the
 diagnostic: evaluate the leak-robust scorer's one-step partial-state
 predictions against AUTHENTIC recorded denoising trajectories vs
 RANDOMLY-REMASKED (artificial-context) states, and report the reward-state
 ALIGNMENT (does the reward track genuine intermediate process quality, not
 reconstructed/leaked context?). Emit reward_state_alignment_passed BARE bool
 := (the scorer's reward correlates with authentic-trajectory process quality
 SIGNIFICANTLY MORE than with randomly-remasked states, CI95-excl-0).
 verifier_is_oracle=false. A pass = the S3 gain is genuine (headline
 graduates); a fail = the gain is alignment-confounded and is QUARANTINED (not
 headline-eligible) + the residual logged as a missing-verifier gap. NO
 training; NO TRM training; DiffusionGemma via the llama.cpp PR binary.

1 of 1 gate(s) failed; first failure: exp4348-s3-stratified-verifier-guided-search.s3_guided_beats_control (actual=False == expected=True)

Co-Authored-By: Codex CLI <noreply@openai.com>
